**Transformation of Trigonometric Integrals**

If \(\tan\frac{u}{2}{=}z\) then

\[\begin{array}{l} {\mbox{\bf 4.3.23}\ \ \sin\ u{=}\frac{2z}{1{+}z^{2}}\ \ \ \cos\ u{=}\frac{1{-}z^{2}}{1{+}z^{2}}\ \ \ du{=}\frac{2}{1{+}z^{2}}\,dz}\end{array}\]

**Multiple-Angle Formulas**

\[\begin{array}{l} {\mbox{\bf 4.3.24}\ \ \sin\ 2z{=}2\ \sin\ z\ \cos\ z{=}\frac{2\tan\ z}{1{+}\tan^{2}z}}\\ {\mbox{\bf 4.3.25}\ \ \cos\ 2z{=}2\ \cos^{2}{-}1{-}2\ \sin^{2}z}\\ {\mbox{\bf =}\cos^{2}{-}\sin^{2}z{=}\frac{1{-}\tan^{2}z}{1{+}\tan^{2}z}} \\ {\mbox{\bf 4.3.26}\ \ \tan\ 2z{=}\frac{2\tan\ z}{1{-}\tan^{2}z}{=}\frac{2\cot\ z}{\cot^{2}z{-}1}{=} \frac{2}{\cot\ z{-}\tan\ z}}\end{array}\]

